# KEYS: lf

## General Navigation

| Key | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| **j** / **k** | Navigate down/up in the file list |
| **h** | Enter parent directory |
| **l** | Open selected directory or file |
| **g** | Go to the top of the file list |
| **G** | Go to the bottom of the file list |
| **Ctrl+f** | Open fuzzy finder (`fzf`) for quick navigation |
| **Ctrl+r** | Reload the current directory |
| **Ctrl+s** | Toggle visibility of hidden files |
| **Ctrl+e** | Scroll one line down |
| **Ctrl+y** | Scroll one line up |
| **V** | Open the current directory in Neovim |

---

## File and Directory Operations

### Basic Management
* **x** - Execute/open selected file with appropriate application
* **o** - Open with default mime application
* **O** - Open with choice of application (mime)
* **D** - Delete selected file(s) or directory(ies) (with confirmation)
* **E** - Extract the selected archive file

### Transfer & Renaming
* **C** - Copy selected items to a specified location
* **M** - Move selected items to a specified location
* **B** - Bulk rename selected files using an external editor
* **b** - Set selected image as wallpaper (requires external script)

---

## Advanced Renaming Bindings

| Key | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| **A** | Rename file with cursor at the **end** of the filename |
| **I** | Rename file with cursor at the **beginning** of the filename |
| **i** | Rename file with cursor just **before the extension** |
| **a** | Rename file with cursor just **after the extension** |
| **c** | Start a new rename operation with an **empty filename** |

---

## Utility & Misc

* **W** - Open a new terminal window (requires `$TERMINAL` env var)
* **Y** - Copy paths of selected file(s) to the system clipboard
* **Ctrl+n** - Create a new directory
* **gh** - Custom user-defined action (mapping)

---

## Configuration

To maintain custom keybindings and shortcuts, ensure your `lfrc` includes:
```bash
source "~/.config/lf/shortcutrc"
```

